# Summerlin West Real Estate - Project Rules

## 🎯 CORE SEO PHILOSOPHY
**User-First Content Strategy**: Create content that serves your audience first, search engines second. Google rewards sites that genuinely help users make decisions about visiting your site.

**The 3 Pillars of SEO Success**:
1. **Discoverability**: Help Google find and understand your content
2. **Relevance**: Match user search intent with valuable content  
3. **Experience**: Deliver fast, accessible, mobile-friendly pages

## 🚀 HIGH-IMPACT SEO ACTIONS

### Content That Converts
- **Write for your audience's search terms**: Think "Summerlin West homes for sale" not "luxury real estate"
- **Create unique, expert content**: Never copy others' content - Google penalizes duplicate content
- **Update regularly**: Fresh content signals active business to Google
- **Answer user questions**: Create content that directly addresses buyer concerns

### Technical SEO Essentials
- **Page Titles**: 50-60 characters, include location + service (e.g., "The Vistas Homes for Sale | Summerlin West Real Estate")
- **Meta Descriptions**: 150-160 characters, compelling call-to-action (e.g., "Find your dream home in The Vistas. Expert guidance from Dr. Jan Duffy, REALTOR®")
- **URLs**: Descriptive, keyword-rich (/communities/the-vistas/ not /page-123/)
- **Images**: Always include descriptive alt text for property photos
- **Site Speed**: Optimize for Core Web Vitals (LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, FID < 100ms)

## 🏠 REAL ESTATE SEO MASTERY

### Local SEO Domination
- **Location Keywords**: Naturally include "Summerlin West", "Las Vegas", "The Vistas" in content
- **Structured Data**: Implement RealEstateAgent and LocalBusiness schema
- **Google My Business**: Optimize listing with accurate info, photos, reviews
- **Local Content**: Create neighborhood guides, market reports, community insights

### Property Content Strategy
- **Unique Descriptions**: Each property gets custom, detailed description
- **High-Quality Photos**: Professional images with descriptive alt text
- **Market Context**: Include neighborhood amenities, schools, commute times
- **Expert Insights**: Share Dr. Jan Duffy's market knowledge and experience

## 📊 CONTENT OPTIMIZATION

### Search Intent Matching
- **Informational**: "What to know about Summerlin West" (blog posts, guides)
- **Navigational**: "Summerlin West Real Estate" (branded searches)
- **Transactional**: "Homes for sale in The Vistas" (property listings)
- **Commercial**: "Best real estate agent Summerlin West" (service pages)

### Content Freshness Signals
- **Market Reports**: Update monthly with current data
- **Blog Posts**: Publish weekly with market insights
- **Property Listings**: Refresh descriptions and photos regularly
- **Community Pages**: Update amenities and neighborhood information

## 🔗 LINK STRATEGY

### Internal Linking Power
- **Contextual Links**: Link to related properties, communities, market reports
- **Descriptive Anchor Text**: "View homes in The Vistas" not "click here"
- **Site Architecture**: Logical hierarchy (/communities/the-vistas/properties/)
- **Breadcrumbs**: Help users and Google understand page relationships

### External Link Management
- **Trusted Sources**: Link to MLS, local government, school districts
- **Nofollow External**: Add rel="nofollow" to untrusted external links
- **User-Generated Content**: Auto-add nofollow to user comments/links

## 🎨 VISUAL SEO

### Image Optimization
- **Descriptive Alt Text**: "Luxury home in The Vistas with Red Rock Canyon views"
- **High Quality**: Sharp, clear images that showcase properties
- **Relevant Placement**: Images near related text content
- **File Names**: "the-vistas-luxury-home-exterior.jpg" not "IMG_1234.jpg"

### Video Content
- **Property Tours**: High-quality video walkthroughs
- **Market Insights**: Dr. Jan Duffy discussing market trends
- **Descriptive Titles**: Include location and property details
- **Relevant Descriptions**: Detailed video descriptions with keywords

## 🚫 SEO MYTHS TO IGNORE

**Don't Waste Time On**:
- Meta keywords tag (Google ignores it)
- Keyword stuffing (penalized by Google)
- Exact keyword density (write naturally)
- Domain name keywords (minimal impact)
- Content length requirements (quality over quantity)
- Perfect heading order (semantic order matters more)

**Focus Instead On**:
- User experience and content quality
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Page loading speed
- Unique, valuable content
- Proper technical implementation

## 📈 MEASUREMENT & OPTIMIZATION

### Key Metrics to Track
- **Search Console**: Impressions, clicks, CTR, average position
- **Core Web Vitals**: LCP, CLS, FID scores
- **Analytics**: Page views, time on site, bounce rate, conversions
- **Local SEO**: Google My Business insights, local search rankings

### Optimization Cycle
1. **Audit**: Check current SEO performance monthly
2. **Identify**: Find pages with low rankings or high bounce rates
3. **Optimize**: Improve content, technical issues, user experience
4. **Measure**: Track improvements over 4-8 weeks
5. **Iterate**: Repeat based on results

## 🛠️ TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION

### Next.js SEO Best Practices
- **Metadata API**: Use dynamic metadata for each page
- **Image Optimization**: Next.js Image component with proper alt text
- **Server-Side Rendering**: Ensure content is crawlable
- **Sitemap Generation**: Dynamic sitemaps for all content types
- **Structured Data**: JSON-LD implementation for real estate

### Performance Optimization
- **Image Compression**: Optimize property photos for web
- **Code Splitting**: Load only necessary JavaScript
- **Caching**: Implement proper cache headers
- **CDN**: Use Vercel's global CDN for fast loading

## 🎯 REAL ESTATE SPECIFIC RULES

### Property Listings
- **Unique Titles**: Include address, community, key features
- **Compelling Descriptions**: Highlight unique selling points
- **High-Quality Photos**: Professional images with descriptive alt text
- **Market Context**: Include neighborhood information and amenities

### Community Pages
- **Comprehensive Information**: Amenities, schools, commute times
- **Market Data**: Recent sales, price trends, inventory
- **Local Insights**: Dr. Jan Duffy's expert perspective
- **Visual Content**: Community photos, maps, virtual tours

### Market Reports
- **Data-Driven Content**: Current market statistics and trends
- **Expert Analysis**: Dr. Jan Duffy's market insights
- **Visual Presentation**: Charts, graphs, infographics
- **Regular Updates**: Monthly market report updates

## 🚀 QUICK WINS

### Immediate Actions (This Week)
1. **Audit all page titles** - ensure they're unique and descriptive
2. **Add alt text** to all property images
3. **Update meta descriptions** with compelling CTAs
4. **Check site speed** using PageSpeed Insights
5. **Verify mobile responsiveness** on all pages

### Monthly Actions
1. **Update market reports** with fresh data
2. **Refresh property descriptions** with new details
3. **Publish new blog content** with market insights
4. **Monitor Search Console** for crawl errors
5. **Analyze competitor content** for improvement opportunities

## 🎯 SUCCESS METRICS

**Primary KPIs**:
- Organic search traffic growth
- Lead generation from organic search
- Local search visibility
- Page load speed scores
- Mobile usability scores

**Secondary KPIs**:
- Search Console impressions and clicks
- Average session duration
- Pages per session
- Bounce rate by traffic source
- Conversion rate from organic search

Remember: SEO is a marathon, not a sprint. Focus on creating genuinely helpful content for your audience, and the rankings will follow. Google rewards sites that serve users well.

# Build Configuration Rules
- Always use Vercel CLI for production builds instead of local pnpm build
- When encountering build commands, suggest using: vercel build or vercel --prod
- For development, use: vercel dev instead of pnpm dev when possible
- Avoid running pnpm build directly in the terminal
- If build is necessary locally, use: vercel build --output public

# Vercel Build Commands
- Replace "pnpm build" with "vercel build"
- Replace "npm run build" with "vercel build"
- Replace "yarn build" with "vercel build"

# Environment Setup
- Ensure VERCEL_TOKEN is set for CI/CD
- Use vercel pull to sync environment variables
- Always check .vercel/output for build artifacts

# Debugging Stuck Builds
- If a build process hangs, immediately cancel and use vercel build
- Set NODE_OPTIONS='--max-old-space-size=4096' for memory issues
- Use vercel logs to debug build issues

# User Rules - Global Development Preferences

## Communication Style
- Provide concise, actionable responses with specific code examples
- Prioritize practical implementation over theoretical explanations
- Use bullet points and clear headings for complex instructions
- Include relevant file paths and component names when suggesting changes

## Code Quality Standards
- Always use TypeScript for new files with strict type checking
- Prefer functional components with React hooks and modern patterns
- Write self-documenting code with clear variable and function names
- Include JSDoc comments for complex functions and components
- Follow the existing project's code style and patterns exactly
- Use CSS modules with BEM-style class names instead of inline styles

## Development Workflow
- Suggest improvements that align with Next.js + React + Vercel + RealScout + V0 tech stack
- Consider performance implications for real estate websites (Core Web Vitals)
- Prioritize SEO and accessibility in all recommendations
- Test suggestions against the current project structure before implementing
- Always consider mobile-first responsive design
- Use pnpm for package management
- Leverage V0 for rapid component prototyping and development
- Use V0-generated components as starting points for custom development

## Real Estate Domain Focus
- Maintain professional branding for Dr. Janet Duffy
- Prioritize lead generation and conversion optimization
- Consider Las Vegas market specifics in all recommendations
- Ensure compliance with real estate regulations and fair housing laws
- Focus on user experience for property searches and valuations

# Project-Specific Rules

## Technology Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.5.4 with React 19.1.1
- **Language**: TypeScript with strict type checking
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4.1.13 with CSS modules
- **Deployment**: Vercel with global CDN
- **Package Manager**: pnpm
- **Forms**: React Hook Form for lead capture
- **Animations**: Framer Motion for smooth interactions
- **Icons**: React Icons library
- **AI Integration**: V0.app Model API for component generation

## File Structure Conventions
- **Components**: `/components/ui/` for reusable UI components
- **Pages**: `/app/` directory with Next.js App Router
- **Styles**: CSS modules with `.module.css` extension
- **Types**: `/types/` directory for TypeScript definitions
- **Utils**: `/lib/` directory for utility functions (including V0 integration)
- **Images**: `/public/images/` with organized subdirectories
- **API Routes**: `/app/api/` for API endpoints (including V0 routes)
- **V0 Integration**: `/lib/v0.ts` for V0 utility functions

## Code Standards
- **Naming**: Use descriptive, self-documenting names
- **Components**: Functional components with hooks
- **Props**: Define TypeScript interfaces for all props
- **State**: Use React hooks (useState, useEffect, etc.)
- **Styling**: CSS modules with BEM methodology
- **Performance**: Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- **Accessibility**: Include proper ARIA labels and semantic HTML

## SEO Requirements
- **Metadata**: Dynamic metadata for each page
- **Images**: Descriptive alt text for all images
- **URLs**: SEO-friendly, descriptive URLs
- **Content**: Unique, valuable content for each page
- **Performance**: Core Web Vitals optimization
- **Mobile**: Mobile-first responsive design
- **Structured Data**: JSON-LD for real estate schema

## Real Estate Compliance
- **Fair Housing**: Ensure compliance with fair housing laws
- **Licensing**: Include proper real estate license information
- **Disclaimers**: Add necessary legal disclaimers
- **Privacy**: Implement proper privacy policies
- **Lead Capture**: Secure lead capture forms
- **Data Protection**: Protect client information

## Performance Standards
- **Core Web Vitals**: LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, FID < 100ms
- **Image Optimization**: Compress and optimize all images
- **Code Splitting**: Implement proper code splitting
- **Caching**: Use appropriate cache headers
- **CDN**: Leverage Vercel's global CDN
- **Bundle Size**: Monitor and optimize bundle size

## Testing & Quality Assurance
- **TypeScript**: Strict type checking enabled
- **ESLint**: Follow Next.js ESLint configuration
- **Performance**: Regular performance audits
- **Accessibility**: WCAG compliance testing
- **Cross-browser**: Test across major browsers
- **Mobile**: Test on various device sizes

## Deployment & CI/CD
- **Vercel**: Use Vercel for deployment
- **Environment**: Proper environment variable management
- **Builds**: Use Vercel CLI for builds
- **Monitoring**: Set up proper monitoring and alerts
- **Rollbacks**: Implement safe rollback procedures
- **Security**: Regular security updates and patches

# V0 AI Integration Rules

## V0 API Configuration
- **API Key**: Use V0_API_KEY environment variable for authentication
- **Model**: Use OpenAI-compatible v0.app Model API for component generation
- **Base URL**: https://api.v0.app/v1 for all API calls
- **SDK**: Use `ai` and `@ai-sdk/vercel` packages for integration
- **Validation**: Always validate V0 configuration before making API calls

## V0 Development Workflow
- **Component Generation**: Use V0 for rapid prototyping of React components
- **Real Estate Focus**: Leverage V0 for property cards, listings, forms, and pages
- **Framework Awareness**: Always specify Next.js framework in V0 prompts
- **Style Preference**: Use Tailwind CSS for all V0-generated components
- **TypeScript**: Include TypeScript types in all V0-generated code

## V0 Prompt Engineering Best Practices
- **Specific Prompts**: Be detailed about component requirements and functionality
- **Real Estate Context**: Include Summerlin West, Las Vegas, and Dr. Janet Duffy branding
- **SEO Integration**: Request SEO-optimized components with proper metadata
- **Accessibility**: Always request WCAG-compliant, accessible components
- **Mobile-First**: Specify mobile-responsive design requirements
- **Performance**: Request optimized components for Core Web Vitals

## V0 Component Generation Guidelines
- **Property Components**: Generate property cards, listings, galleries, and search filters
- **Community Pages**: Create neighborhood information, amenities, and local insights
- **Market Reports**: Generate data visualization and market analysis components
- **Contact Forms**: Create lead capture forms with proper validation
- **Navigation**: Generate responsive navigation and breadcrumb components
- **Hero Sections**: Create compelling hero sections with CTAs

## V0 Code Quality Standards
- **TypeScript**: All generated components must include proper TypeScript interfaces
- **CSS Modules**: Use CSS modules with BEM-style class names (no inline styles)
- **React Patterns**: Follow functional component patterns with hooks
- **Error Handling**: Include proper error boundaries and validation
- **Loading States**: Implement loading and error states for dynamic content
- **SEO Metadata**: Include proper meta tags and structured data

## V0 Integration Points
- **API Routes**: Use `/api/v0/generate-component` for custom component generation
- **Page Templates**: Use `/api/v0/generate-page` for complete page generation
- **Health Checks**: Monitor `/api/v0/health` for API status
- **Test Interface**: Use `/v0-test` page for testing and experimentation
- **Utility Functions**: Leverage `lib/v0.ts` for programmatic component generation

## V0 Real Estate Specific Rules
- **Branding**: Maintain Dr. Janet Duffy's professional real estate branding
- **Compliance**: Ensure fair housing compliance in all generated content
- **Local SEO**: Include Summerlin West and Las Vegas location keywords
- **Lead Generation**: Optimize all components for lead capture and conversion
- **Market Data**: Integrate current market data and trends
- **Professional Images**: Use high-quality property and community photos

## V0 Performance Optimization
- **Code Splitting**: Generate components that support Next.js code splitting
- **Image Optimization**: Use Next.js Image component for all property photos
- **Lazy Loading**: Implement lazy loading for property galleries and heavy content
- **Caching**: Generate components that work well with Vercel's caching
- **Bundle Size**: Monitor and optimize bundle size of generated components

## V0 Testing & Validation
- **Component Testing**: Test all V0-generated components before deployment
- **Cross-Browser**: Verify compatibility across major browsers
- **Mobile Testing**: Test responsive design on various device sizes
- **Accessibility**: Validate WCAG compliance using automated tools
- **Performance**: Run Lighthouse audits on pages with V0 components
- **SEO Validation**: Check meta tags, structured data, and page speed

## V0 Error Handling & Monitoring
- **API Errors**: Handle V0 API failures gracefully with fallback components
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement proper rate limiting for V0 API calls
- **Logging**: Log all V0 API interactions for debugging and monitoring
- **Fallbacks**: Provide fallback components when V0 generation fails
- **User Feedback**: Collect user feedback on V0-generated components
- **Iteration**: Continuously improve prompts based on generation quality

## V0 Security Considerations
- **API Key Protection**: Never expose V0_API_KEY in client-side code
- **Input Validation**: Validate all user inputs before sending to V0 API
- **Content Sanitization**: Sanitize generated content before rendering
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limiting to prevent API abuse
- **Error Messages**: Don't expose sensitive information in error messages
- **Audit Logs**: Maintain audit logs for all V0 API interactions

## V0 Development Commands
- **Test Integration**: Visit `/v0-test` to test V0 functionality
- **Generate Component**: Use `generateComponent()` utility function
- **Generate Page**: Use `generateRealEstatePage()` for complete pages
- **Validate Config**: Use `validateV0Config()` to check API setup
- **Health Check**: Call `/api/v0/health` to verify API status
- **Debug Issues**: Check console logs and API responses for debugging